---
source: crates/onequery-cli/src/cli/../cli_tests.rs
expression: "rendered_display(&[\"onequery\", \"query\", \"exec\", \"--help\"])"
---
Execute a query and return rows

Usage: onequery query exec [OPTIONS] --source <SOURCE> --input <PATH|->
       onequery query exec [OPTIONS] --source <SOURCE> --sql <SQL>
       onequery query exec [OPTIONS] --source <SOURCE> --file <PATH>
       onequery query exec [OPTIONS] --source <SOURCE> --stdin

Options:
      --source <SOURCE>  Execute the query against this source
  -h, --help             Print help
  -V, --version          Print version

Read Controls:
      --fields <FIELDS>  Project only the requested response fields

Pagination:
      --page-size <PAGE_SIZE>  Limit the number of records returned in one page
      --cursor <CURSOR>        Resume listing from this pagination cursor
      --page-all               Continue loading pages until the server is exhausted

Query Input:
      --input <PATH|->  Read a full query request payload from a JSON file or stdin (`-`)
      --sql <SQL>       Provide SQL directly on the command line
      --file <PATH>     Read SQL from a UTF-8 file
      --stdin           Read SQL from stdin

Result Window:
      --max-rows <MAX_ROWS>              Cap the number of rows returned by the query
      --max-bytes <MAX_BYTES>            Cap the total response payload size in bytes
      --cell-max-chars <CELL_MAX_CHARS>  Truncate individual cell values to this many characters
      --timeout-ms <MILLISECONDS>        Override the query execution timeout in milliseconds

Global Options:
      --org <ORG_SLUG>           Override the active org for this invocation
      --profile <PROFILE>        Select a local auth/config profile for this invocation
  -c, --config <KEY=VALUE>       Apply a raw config override for this invocation using `key=value`
      --request-id <REQUEST_ID>  Attach a caller-supplied request ID to outbound API requests
      --timeout <SECONDS>        Override the request timeout in seconds for this invocation
      --json                     Emit machine-readable JSON output
      --text                     Emit human-readable text output
      --verbose                  Emit workflow progress and retry tracing to stderr
